{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9842439c-c366-4aba-9892-f223e02e89c9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-871225c2a38f3cad","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9008-jsho0m0a/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9008-E001.md","content":"# Resolve enterprise admin configuration UX direction (simplification vs. fine-grained controls)\n\n## Description\n\nEnterprise feedback on administration is contradictory: one strategic account\nwants fewer configuration options exposed (\"too many knobs\"), while another\nexplicitly wants more fine-grained controls per project. The feedback arrived\nthrough different channels and has not been consolidated. This investigation\nconsolidates that feedback, determines which direction takes precedence for\nthe RHOAI admin configuration experience (or whether a blended approach is\nviable), and produces a decision record that determines which implementation\nwork is executed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Consolidate all field/account feedback channels contributing to the\n  admin-usability complaints into a single inventory with attributed use\n  cases.\n- Identify the conflicting accounts and characterize the workflows behind\n  each ask (operator vs. project-admin vs. end-user perspective).\n- Evaluate the candidate directions against the existing Dashboard admin\n  configuration model (settings administered through the Dashboard\n  configuration CR and surfaced in the console).\n- Produce a decision record selecting one of: (a) simplify the exposed\n  configuration with curated defaults, (b) add fine-grained per-project\n  administrative controls, or (c) a blended approach.\n- Enumerate the resulting implementation scope (which admin configuration\n  surfaces change under the selected direction).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- All feedback channels contributing to the \"too many knobs\" vs.\n  \"fine-grained controls\