{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bab4aae4baf044d3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n3\tepic_count: 6\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9008\n11\t\n12\tStrategy: \"Make RHOAI more usable for enterprise teams\" (status: Refinement\n13\tDone, priority: Normal).\n14\t\n15\t## Triage Outcome\n16\t\n17\tNeither Step 0 check fired:\n18\t\n19\t- **Not below threshold**: the strategy is not S-sized — it spans two\n20\t  components (Dashboard, Notebooks), two owning teams, and contains three\n21\t  genuine unknowns (the Open Questions table) whose answers change which epics\n22\t  exist and what they do. The \"genuine unknowns\" escape condition applies.\n23\t- **Not docs-only**: Dashboard and Notebooks are code-bearing components with\n24\t  active changes implied by HLR-1..HLR-3; only HLR-4 is documentation work.\n25\t\n26\tFull decomposition follows.\n27\t\n28\t## Strategy Structure Notes (Step 1 / Step 1.5)\n29\t\n30\tParsed: Problem Statement, High-Level Requirements (HLR-1..HLR-4), Affected\n31\tComponents (Dashboard, Notebooks), Out of Scope (empty), Open Questions (3).\n32\t\n33\t**Missing sections** (health warnings, work proceeded with available info):\n34\tImpacted Teams table, Dependencies table, Acceptance Criteria (no\n35\tGiven/When/Then with \"measured by\" clauses), Non-Functional Requirements, and\n36\tStaff Engineer Input. Owning teams were inferred from\n37\t`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`\n38\t(RHOAI Dashboard) and `notebooks.md` (Workbenches).\n39\t\n40\t**Priority note**: HLR-1, HLR-2 and HLR-3 carry no priority (\"—\"); the only\n41\texplicit priority in the strategy is HLR-4 (P2). The unprioritized core HLRs\n42\twere defaulted to **P1** (core value delivery, leadership wants visible\n43\tprogress) — flagged as a health warning for human confirmation.\n44\t\n45\t**Component mapping**: \"Dashboard\" and \"Notebooks\" are canonical names in\n46\t`.context/rhai-components.txt` — no mapping needed. Both components exist in\n47\tarchitecture context (both GA, both Konflux-onboarded) — no new-component\n48\tonboarding chain is required (Rule 20 does not apply). The whitepaper epic\n49\tuses the canonical \"Documentation\" component; its team (\"RHOAI\n50\tDocumentation\") is inferred because the strategy has no Impacted Teams table.\n51\t\n52\t## Epic List\n53\t\n54\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n55\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n56\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E001 | Resolve enterprise admin configuration UX direction (simplification vs. fine-grained controls) | Investigation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n57\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E002 | Define data-scientist onboarding scope and baseline first-day time breakdown | Investigation | Workbenches | P1 |\n58\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E003 | Identify target enterprise tooling for RHOAI integration | Investigation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n59\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E004 | Reduce data-scientist onboarding time to under one day | Implementation | Workbenches | P1 |\n60\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E005 | Integrate RHOAI with prioritized enterprise tooling | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n61\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-E006 | Publish enterprise usability best-practices whitepaper | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P2 |\n62\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-BRANCH-A-E007 | Implement simplified enterprise admin configuration experience | Implementation (branch A) | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n63\t| RHAISTRAT-9008-BRANCH-B-E007 | Implement fine-grained per-project administrative controls | Implementation (branch B) | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n64\t\n65\tBranch epics are conditional outcomes of E001 (see \"Conditional Branches\").\n66\t`epic_count` counts the 6 main-plan epics; branch epics are excluded from the\n67\tmain-plan critical path.\n68\t\n69\t## Dependency DAG\n70\t\n71\t```mermaid\n72\tgraph TD\n73\t    E001[\"E001 Investigation: admin UX direction\"]\n74\t    E002[\"E002 Investigation: onboarding scope/baseline\"]\n75\t    E003[\"E003 Investigation: enterprise tooling targets\"]\n76\t    E004[\"E004 Implementation: onboarding time reduction\"]\n77\t    E005[\"E005 Implementation: enterprise tooling integration\"]\n78\t    E006[\"E006 docs-authoring: whitepaper\"]\n79\t    BA[\"BRANCH-A-E007 simplified admin config (if E001 -> simplification)\"]\n80\t    BB[\"BRANCH-B-E007 fine-grained controls (if E001 -> granularity)\"]\n81\t\n82\t    E001 --> BA\n83\t    E001 --> BB\n84\t    E002 --> E004\n85\t    E003 --> E005\n86\t    E001 --> E006\n87\t    E004 --> E006\n88\t    E005 --> E006\n89\t```\n90\t\n91\tArrows point from dependency to dependent (\"E001 --> E006\" means E001 must\n92\tcomplete before E006 starts).\n93\t\n94\t## DAG Justification\n95\t\n96\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n97\t|------|------|-----------|\n98\t| E001 → BRANCH-A-E007 | Rule 3 | The admin-UX direction decision determines whether the simplification implementation exists at all; bounded outcome (2 possibilities) → conditional branch. True gate, action `remove`. |\n99\t| E001 → BRANCH-B-E007 | Rule 3 | Same gate, opposite outcome; true gate, action `remove`. |\n100\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 3 | Onboarding scope/baseline defines what E004 builds and where; outcome is unbounded (>3 possible scopes) → main-plan epic gated with `rewrite`. True gate. |\n101\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 3 | Tool identification determines whether E005 exists and what it integrates; unbounded outcome → gated with `rewrite`. True gate. |\n102\t| E004 → E006 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring epic is blocked by all main-plan Implementation epics; docs describe what was built. |\n103\t| E005 → E006 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n104\t| E001 → E006 | Rule 11 (extension) | The whitepaper must reflect the resolved admin-UX direction. The HLR-1 implementations live in branches (which main-plan epics must not depend on), so the gating Investigation E001 stands in as the main-plan dependency for that outcome. |\n105\t| E001 ∥ E002 ∥ E003 | Rule 14/15 | The three investigations are independent (different unknowns, different deliverables, different resolution methods); they run in parallel. |\n106\t| E004 ∥ E005 | Rule 14/15 | Different components/teams/repos, no shared artifacts → parallel. |\n107\t| No konflux edges | Rule 10 | Both components are already Konflux-onboarded (architecture context); no `konflux-onboarding` epic exists in any dependency chain, so Rule 25's \"build pipeline green\" AC is not triggered. |\n108\t\n109\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n110\t\n111\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n112\t|-----|----------|-------|\n113\t| HLR-1 (simpler administration; conflicting feedback) | — (defaulted P1) | E001 (Investigation), BRANCH-A-E007 / BRANCH-B-E007 (conditional implementations) |\n114\t| HLR-2 (data-scientist onboarding < 1 day) | — (defaulted P1) | E002 (Investigation), E004 (Implementation) |\n115\t| HLR-3 (better enterprise tooling integration) | — (defaulted P1) | E003 (Investigation), E005 (Implementation) |\n116\t| HLR-4 (enterprise usability whitepaper) | P2 | E006 (docs-authoring) |\n117\t\n118\tAll HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. HLR-4's P2 does not propagate\n119\tupstream (docs-authoring priority exception); E006's priority derives from the\n120\tstrategy frontmatter `priority: Normal` → P2.\n121\t\n122\t## Conditional Branches\n123\t\n124\tE001's outcome is bounded (≤3 possibilities), so the HLR-1 implementation work\n125\tis expressed as conditional branch epics rather than a main-plan epic:\n126\t\n127\t- **Branch A — simplification wins** (`RHAISTRAT-9008-BRANCH-A-E007.md`):\n128\t  fewer exposed admin configuration options with curated defaults. Replaces\n129\t  part of the existing admin configuration exposure → Rule 23 rollback /\n130\t  feature-flag AC included.\n131\t- **Branch B — granularity wins** (`RHAISTRAT-9008-BRANCH-B-E007.md`):\n132\t  fine-grained per-project administrative controls layered on the existing\n133\t  platform-wide settings. Rule 23 rollback / feature-flag AC included (it\n134\t  reshapes the admin configuration surface).\n135\t\n136\tA blended resolution (e.g. progressive disclosure of both) would be handled as\n137\ta `rewrite` of whichever branch is closer; both branch files record\n138\t`gate_failure_impact.action=remove` for the non-selected outcome. Branch epics\n139\tset `branch`, `gated_by=E001` (also in `dependencies`), and no main-plan epic\n140\tdepends on them.\n141\t\n142\t## Health Warnings\n143\t\n144\t1. **Missing strategy sections**: Impacted Teams, Dependencies, Acceptance\n145\t   Criteria, NFRs and Staff Engineer Input are absent; teams were inferred\n146\t   from architecture context. The review should verify team assignments.\n147\t2. **HLR-1 is self-contradictory** (one account wants fewer knobs, another\n148\t   wants more fine-grained controls). Handled as a bounded Investigation with\n149\t   conditional branches rather than an arbitrary pick.\n150\t3. **Unprioritized core HLRs**: HLR-1..HLR-3 have no priority; defaulted to\n151\t   P1. Only HLR-4 is explicitly prioritized (P2). Possible priority inversion\n152\t   risk: leadership wants \"visible usability progress this release\", yet the\n153\t   decomposition is investigation-heavy — the first release-visible\n154\t   implementations (E004, E005, branch work) cannot start until the\n155\t   investigations resolve.\n156\t4. **Scope trap**: \"Out of Scope: nothing has been explicitly scoped out\"\n157\t   combined with undefined HLR-2 scope (\"onboarding\" undefined) and unnamed\n158\t   HLR-3 tools means the strategy's actual implementation surface is\n159\t   unbounded. Mitigated by gating E004/E005 on E002/E003 with `rewrite`\n160\t   impacts.\n161\t5. **HLR-2 has no baseline or measurable definition** (\"less than a day\" with\n162\t   no definition of onboarding or where the day is spent). E002 must produce\n163\t   the definition and baseline before E004's target is measurable.\n164\t6. **Strategy contains no acceptance criteria** — all epic acceptance criteria\n165\t   below were derived from HLR text and standard rules (23-25), not from\n166\t   strategy-level Given/When/Then clauses.\n167\t\n168\t## Tiered Delivery\n169\t\n170\tNot applicable: no external dependency with uncertain timing exists. All\n171\tgates are internal investigations.\n172\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4fedbb549889118","agent_id":"a96fc96f9a143a395","session_id":"75f31b44-6829-4bc6-8c24-b6fae2a504e2","uuid":"526be1ac-11fa-445c-99d4-72d141be05bf","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:58:43.873Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bab4aae4baf044d3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
