{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81c92885ec249ab7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E001\n3\ttitle: Resolve enterprise admin configuration UX direction (simplification vs. fine-grained\n4\t  controls)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n6\tcomponent: Dashboard\n7\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Low\n20\tai_implementability_score: -1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Resolve enterprise admin configuration UX direction (simplification vs. fine-grained controls)\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tEnterprise feedback on administration is contradictory: one strategic account\n31\twants fewer configuration options exposed (\"too many knobs\"), while another\n32\texplicitly wants more fine-grained controls per project. The feedback arrived\n33\tthrough different channels and has not been consolidated. This investigation\n34\tconsolidates that feedback, determines which direction takes precedence for\n35\tthe RHOAI admin configuration experience (or whether a blended approach is\n36\tviable), and produces a decision record that determines which implementation\n37\twork is executed.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Consolidate all field/account feedback channels contributing to the\n42\t  admin-usability complaints into a single inventory with attributed use\n43\t  cases.\n44\t- Identify the conflicting accounts and characterize the workflows behind\n45\t  each ask (operator vs. project-admin vs. end-user perspective).\n46\t- Evaluate the candidate directions against the existing Dashboard admin\n47\t  configuration model (settings administered through the Dashboard\n48\t  configuration CR and surfaced in the console).\n49\t- Produce a decision record selecting one of: (a) simplify the exposed\n50\t  configuration with curated defaults, (b) add fine-grained per-project\n51\t  administrative controls, or (c) a blended approach.\n52\t- Enumerate the resulting implementation scope (which admin configuration\n53\t  surfaces change under the selected direction).\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- All feedback channels contributing to the \"too many knobs\" vs.\n58\t  \"fine-grained controls\" conflict are consolidated into a single inventory\n59\t  with attributed use cases — no known channel is left unconsolidated.\n60\t- A documented decision selects one direction (or a justified blend), with\n61\t  rationale tied to account impact and measured against the platform's\n62\t  existing admin configuration surfaces.\n63\t- The implementation scope for the selected direction is enumerated\n64\t  (configuration surfaces affected, expected user-visible change), sufficient\n65\t  to start implementation without a further discovery step.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (administration should be simpler; conflicting account feedback) —\n70\t  this investigation resolves the open question of which feedback takes\n71\t  precedence; the resulting implementation work is selected conditionally on\n72\t  the outcome.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4fedbb549889118","agent_id":"a96fc96f9a143a395","session_id":"75f31b44-6829-4bc6-8c24-b6fae2a504e2","uuid":"4df745d4-9013-4b5b-be8b-612f48cd2ebe","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:58:48.253Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-81c92885ec249ab7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
