{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b10afcb714e8e098","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E003\n3\ttitle: Identify target enterprise tooling for RHOAI integration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 0\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Identify target enterprise tooling for RHOAI integration\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThe strategy asks that the platform \"integrate better\" with existing\n30\tenterprise tooling, but no specific tools were named in the consolidated\n31\tfeedback. This investigation determines which enterprise tools the strategic\n32\taccounts actually mean, validates the demand, and produces a prioritized\n33\tshortlist with a mapping of where each integration would land in the platform\n34\t— the deliverable that determines whether integration work exists and what it\n35\ttargets.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Consolidate which enterprise tools the strategic accounts and field teams\n40\t  refer to (e.g., identity providers, source control, ticketing, monitoring,\n41\t  data platforms), with the originating account attributed.\n42\t- Validate demand per candidate tool (how many accounts, what workflow the\n43\t  integration unblocks).\n44\t- Assess feasibility per candidate: which platform surface the integration\n45\t  would touch (console experience, authentication, workbench environment,\n46\t  serving/pipeline integrations) and any upstream or vendor coordination it\n47\t  requires.\n48\t- Produce a prioritized integration shortlist with recommended integration\n49\t  surface and rough effort per entry, sufficient to scope implementation.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A candidate tool list exists with attributed demand per strategic account —\n54\t  no known feedback channel is left unconsolidated.\n55\t- Each shortlisted tool has a mapped integration surface in the platform and\n56\t  a stated feasibility assessment (including any upstream/vendor dependency).\n57\t- A prioritized shortlist with a documented ranking rationale is produced and\n58\t  agreed with product stakeholders.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-3 (the platform should integrate better with existing enterprise\n63\t  tooling) — this investigation resolves the open question of which tools are\n64\t  actually meant; downstream integration work is gated on its outcome.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4fedbb549889118","agent_id":"a96fc96f9a143a395","session_id":"75f31b44-6829-4bc6-8c24-b6fae2a504e2","uuid":"facf25d9-00ca-459f-b688-e366f41928c7","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:58:50.084Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b10afcb714e8e098","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
