epics and\n171\tevery frontmatter value matches its rationale.\n172\t\n173\tSpot-checks against the rubrics: E001's `human_judgment_required: -2` is\n174\tcorrect (the gating question — which contradictory account requirement wins\n175\t— is itself a stakeholder decision); E001/E003's `source_accessibility: 0`\n176\tis correct (the answers live in unconsolidated field feedback, not readable\n177\tartifacts); E002's `cluster_hardware_dependence: -1` correctly distinguishes\n178\tthe peripheral baseline measurement (needs a live cluster) from the gating\n179\tscope-definition question; E004/E005's `open_questions: -1` correctly\n180\treflects the gating unresolved questions; both branches' `pattern_precedent:\n181\t1` and `architecture_claims: 1` are substantiated by the Dashboard\n182\t(OdhDashboardConfig CR) and Notebooks (culling defaults with per-workbench\n183\toverrides) architecture context files; E006's `human_process_gates: -1`\n184\tcorrectly captures the docs-content review/sign-off process, and its\n185\t`open_questions: 0` rationale (upstream uncertainty captured as DAG\n186\tdependencies, not in-epic design decisions) is sound.\n187\t\n188\tOne borderline value: E002's `source_accessibility: 1` — the onboarding\n189\tjourney structure is determinable from readable artifacts, but the measured\n190\ttime baseline is not (that part needs a cluster and observation). The\n191\trationale is honest about the split and the value is defensible for the\n192\tgating question; this is the kind of arguable-but-reasonable call the rubric\n193\tpermits without penalty.\n194\t\n195\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n196\t\n197\tEvery epic has testable acceptance criteria derived from the HLR text and\n198\tstrategy context. All rule-mandated ACs are present wherever the rule's\n199\ttrigger condition holds:\n200\t\n201\t- Rule 23 (replacement/reshaping of existing capability → rollback /\n202\t  feature-flag AC): BRANCH-A-E007 and BRANCH-B-E007 each carry an explicit\n203\t  feature-flag/rollback AC (\"reverting restores the previously exposed\n204\t  configuration surface\" / \"restores the prior platform-wide-only\n205\t  configuration behavior\"); E004 carries a reversibility AC for changed\n206\t  defaults; E005 carries an additive-behavior-preserved AC.\n207\t- Rule 24 (docs-authoring → technically reviewed against implementation):\n208\t  E006's second AC requires technical review \"against the implemented\n209\t  platform behavior ... by someone with knowledge of the implementations,\n210\t  with review comments resolved.\"\n211\t- Rule 25 (konflux in dependency chain → build pipeline green): correctly\n212\t  not triggered — no konflux-onboarding epic exists in any chain.\n213\t\n214\tACs are concretely testable where the strategy permits (e.g., E004's\n215\t\"measured across the defined onboarding scope and with the same measurement\n216\tmethod as the baseline, is under one day\"; E002's \"measured on a\n217\trepresentative cluster configuration rather than estimated\"). No epic body\n218\treferences sibling epics by draft ID — all cross-epic references use plain\n219\tterms (\"the onboarding definition and baseline\", \"the direction decision\",\n220\t\"the tooling identification work\"). Zero draft-ID references across all\n221\teight epic bodies.\n222\t\n223\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n224\t\n225\tAll strategy scope is accounted for. Each of the three strategy open\n226\tquestions maps to exactly one Investigation epic (Q1→E001, Q2→E002, Q3→E003)\n227\t— the \"genuine unknowns\" escape from triage was correctly applied since each\n228\tanswer changes which epics exist or what they do. The problem statement's\n229\tunconsolidated-feedback concern is carried as consolidation scope in E001\n230\tand E003. \"Leadership wants visible usability progress this release\" is\n231\tcarried forward as health warning 3 (investigation-heavy structure vs.\n232\trelease visibility). The empty out-of-scope section is flagged as a scope\n233\ttrap (health warning 4) with mitigation via the rewrite gates on E004/E005.\n234\tThe contradiction inside HLR-1 is handled by the bounded Investigation +\n235\tconditional branches rather than an arbitrary pick, and all three outcomes\n236\tare covered: simplification (branch A), granularity (branch B), and blend\n237\t(documented as a rewrite of the nearer branch, with both branch files\n238\trecording `action=remove` for the non-selected outcome).\n239\t\n240\tHLR-4's whitepaper requirement has its dedicated docs-authoring epic (the\n241\tstrategy has no Prerequisites & Process Gates section, so the\n242\tDocumentation-Support trigger does not apply, but the explicit HLR makes the\n243\tepic mandatory regardless — and it exists). No capability, acceptance\n244\tcriterion, or stakeholder concern from the strategy is silently dropped.\n245\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89d21299ae8b2e2c","agent_id":"a4c0607f6ac3f8f22","session_id":"75f31b44-6829-4bc6-8c24-b6fae2a504e2","uuid":"8fbd4d08-e061-4f1a-88ec-f75b0c037ddc","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:06:06.381Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-948fa35a09e93e46","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
