{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0509634d7198e9e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9008-E002\n3\ttitle: Define data-scientist onboarding scope and baseline first-day time breakdown\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9008\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks\n6\tteam: Workbenches\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Define data-scientist onboarding scope and baseline first-day time breakdown\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThe strategy requires that onboarding a new data scientist take \"less than a\n30\tday\", but it is not defined what onboarding includes (cluster access, project\n31\tsetup, first workbench, or first deployed model) or where the day is currently\n32\tspent. This investigation defines the onboarding boundary, measures the\n33\tcurrent-state baseline, and produces a ranked list of friction points — the\n34\tdeliverables that determine what onboarding-improvement work is built and\n35\twhere it targets.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Define the onboarding journey boundary for a new data scientist: which\n40\t  stages are in scope (account/cluster access, project setup, first workbench\n41\t  spawn, first deployed model) and which are explicitly out of scope.\n42\t- Measure where a new data scientist's first day is currently spent, per\n43\t  stage, producing a baseline time breakdown.\n44\t- Identify and rank the dominant friction points in the in-scope stages\n45\t  (e.g., workbench provisioning wait time, configuration discovery,\n46\t  permissions hurdles), based on the measured baseline.\n47\t- Produce a measurable onboarding target statement consistent with the\n48\t  \"less than a day\" requirement.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- The onboarding definition enumerates the stages in and out of scope, with\n53\t  rationale, and is agreed with product stakeholders.\n54\t- A baseline time breakdown per in-scope stage exists, measured on a\n55\t  representative cluster configuration rather than estimated.\n56\t- The top friction points are identified and ranked by contribution to total\n57\t  onboarding time, with enough detail to scope remediation work.\n58\t- The \"less than a day\" target is restated as a measurable criterion against\n59\t  the defined scope (which stages it covers and how it is measured).\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-2 (onboarding a new data scientist should take less than a day) — this\n64\t  investigation resolves the open questions of what onboarding covers and\n65\t  where the day is currently spent; downstream implementation scope is\n66\t  determined by its outcome.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89d21299ae8b2e2c","agent_id":"a4c0607f6ac3f8f22","session_id":"75f31b44-6829-4bc6-8c24-b6fae2a504e2","uuid":"9a5e4489-cacf-4408-9b31-dffba40478cf","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:06:18.359Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0509634d7198e9e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9008 decomposition"}
